<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#10132f">
  <title>API Documentation | Husky_dev CDN</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <header class="header">
    <div class="header__logo">API Documentation</div>
  </header>

  <main class="main">
    <section class="section">
      <h1 class="section__title">Direct-to-R2 uploads</h1>
      <p class="section__description">
        The browser sends file bytes directly to Cloudflare R2. The Express function receives only small JSON
        requests and saves verified file metadata to MongoDB.
      </p>
      <p class="section__description">
        Temporary uploads are public. Permanent uploads require an account and active admin-approved permission
        ($5 USD/month); API clients use their account API key.
      </p>

      <div class="section__endpoint">
        <h2 class="endpoint__title">1. Request a presigned URL</h2>
        <code class="endpoint__code">POST /api/presign</code>
        <p class="section__description">
          JSON body: <code>filename</code>, <code>contentType</code>, <code>size</code>, and optional
          <code>expiresIn</code> (<code>12h</code> by default).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="section__endpoint">
        <h2 class="endpoint__title">2. Upload to R2</h2>
        <code class="endpoint__code">PUT &lt;uploadUrl&gt;</code>
        <p class="section__description">Send the file as the request body and the same <code>Content-Type</code>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="section__endpoint">
        <h2 class="endpoint__title">3. Save metadata</h2>
        <code class="endpoint__code">POST /api/files</code>
        <p class="section__description">
          JSON body: <code>intentId</code>. The server checks the R2 object's actual size and content type before
          recording it in MongoDB.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="section__parameters">
        <h2 class="parameters__title">Limits and lifetimes</h2>
        <ul class="parameters__list">
          <li class="parameters__item">Allowed lifetimes: <code>30m</code>, <code>2h</code>, <code>12h</code>, <code>2d</code>, <code>30d</code>, <code>1y</code>, and <code>never</code>.</li>
          <li class="parameters__item">Direct uploads default to 5 GB per file. Set <code>MAX_R2_UPLOAD_SIZE</code> in bytes to lower the limit (maximum 5 GB per PUT).</li>
          <li class="parameters__item">Uploads are limited to 20 requests per IP every 15 minutes and 100 per IP per day. Monthly R2 safety limits can also pause uploads and downloads.</li>
          <li class="parameters__item">Files over 1 GB trigger an admin email alert before upload authorization.</li>
          <li class="parameters__item">User storage remains subject to the 100 GB account quota.</li>
          <li class="parameters__item">Presigned URLs expire after 5 minutes and are restricted to the requested size and content type. The upload request must also send the returned signed headers.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="section__example">
        <h2 class="example__title">Browser example</h2>
        <div class="code-container">
          <pre><code class="language-javascript">const contentType = file.type || 'application/octet-stream'
const presignResponse = await fetch('/api/presign', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    filename: file.name,
    contentType,
    size: file.size,
    expiresIn: '12h'
  })
})
const presign = await presignResponse.json()

if (!presignResponse.ok || !presign.status) throw new Error(presign.message)
await fetch(presign.data.uploadUrl, {
  method: 'PUT',
  headers: presign.data.uploadHeaders,
  body: file
})

const savedResponse = await fetch('/api/files', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ intentId: presign.data.intentId })
})
const saved = await savedResponse.json()
window.location.href = saved.data.pageUrl</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="section__errors">
        <h2 class="errors__title">Legacy API endpoints</h2>
        <p class="section__description">
          <code>POST /api/upload</code> and <code>GET /api/upload/to</code> still use the server-side legacy
          upload flow and remain subject to Vercel's request and function limits. Use the presigned flow above
          for large browser uploads.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <p class="footer__text">© 2026 Husky_dev CDN. All rights reserved. | by <a href="https://github.com/Husky_dev" class="footer__link">Husky_dev</a></p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
